      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name}, I don't think this is the same issue as my post. In my post I use the VRChat input events, but as far as I know, there's no VRChat input event for \"T\", so in this post they must be using something like Unity's Input.GetKeyDown function, which isn't necessarily managed by VRChat. The VRChat input events aren't called when you have menus open.\n\nI was thinking it would be nicer to separate the issues since I believe they stem from different causes. If you just wanted to merge it since you wanted to group together related ones that's fine, I just think it's worth noting that they aren't the same.",
